RE-OWN CLOSURE QA — "Bot Mode" on advance.html (Mission Control group chat). Your QA & integration verification task was cancelled last cycle before completion; re-open it and drive it to closure. You must return a complete closure report in your reply.

WHAT TO DO:
1. Rebuild/refresh the acceptance checklist for the Bot Mode feature (based on your existing delivery plan from the coordination task):
   (a) "🤖 Bot Mode" toggle button exists and is visible in the chat header of advance.html;
   (b) Toggling ON starts an automatic bot-to-bot conversation;
   (c) The 6 bots take turns and reply in their distinct personas (NinjaNerd, ClickClack, Mark, Meta, Manny, Seleena);
   (d) Stop conditions work: max-turns limit, toggle OFF stops the loop, human message interrupts;
   (e) advance.html chat functions normally when Bot Mode is OFF;
   (f) No branding violations (Z-Dot only, no LPT mix).
2. Coordinate with the CTO (NinjaNerd) on the current build status for advance.html. If the build has been delivered, verify each criterion against it and mark PASS/FAIL with evidence. If the build is NOT yet delivered, do NOT pretend it passed — report status BLOCKED and list the exact missing deliverable(s) so the CEO can escalate.
3. Update the project tracker with the current status of the Bot Mode goal (what's done, in progress, blocked) and the next steps.
4. RETURN in your reply: the final closure report (feature verdict: PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED per criterion, with evidence), plus the updated tracker summary.

QA STATUS REQUEST — "Bot Mode" feature on advance.html (Mission Control group chat). I am re-opening the QA & integration verification that was cancelled last cycle and need a precise build status to drive it to closure.

Please report back, with evidence, on the following:

1. BUILD STATUS: Has the advance.html build containing the "🤖 Bot Mode" feature been delivered? If yes, provide the exact deliverable location (file path / branch / commit hash / version), timestamp of delivery, and who delivered it.
2. IMPLEMENTATION COVERAGE — for each of the following acceptance criteria, state whether it is implemented, partially implemented, or NOT implemented, with specifics:
   (a) "🤖 Bot Mode" toggle button exists and is visible in the chat header of advance.html;
   (b) Toggling ON starts an automatic bot-to-bot conversation;
   (c) The 6 bots take turns and reply in their distinct personas (NinjaNerd, ClickClack, Mark, Meta, Manny, Seleena);
   (d) Stop conditions work: max-turns limit, toggle OFF stops the loop, human message interrupts the loop;
   (e) advance.html chat functions normally when Bot Mode is OFF;
   (f) No branding violations (Z-Dot only, no LPT mix).
3. KNOWN ISSUES / BLOCKERS: Any known defects, unmerged changes, or dependencies that would prevent PASS on any criterion.
4. TEST EVIDENCE: Any test runs, screenshots, or QA notes already produced for this feature.

Reply with a structured status so I can update the tracker and produce the closure report. If the build is not delivered, list the exact missing deliverables.

BUILD DELIVERY CROSS-CHECK — "Bot Mode" feature on advance.html (Mission Control group chat). I am the PM re-opening QA on this feature and need a delivery cross-check from the implementation owner.

Please confirm:

1. Did you build and deliver the "🤖 Bot Mode" feature for advance.html? If yes, give the exact deliverable location (file path, branch, commit hash/version), the timestamp of delivery, and to whom it was handed off (CTO approval? staging? production?).
2. Is the delivered code complete and deployable, or is any part still in progress / on a feature branch / unmerged?
3. For each acceptance criterion below, state: IMPLEMENTED / PARTIAL / NOT IMPLEMENTED, with one line of specifics:
   (a) "🤖 Bot Mode" toggle button visible in the chat header of advance.html;
   (b) Toggling ON starts an automatic bot-to-bot conversation;
   (c) 6 bots take turns in distinct personas (NinjaNerd, ClickClack, Mark, Meta, Manny, Seleena);
   (d) Stop conditions: max-turns limit, toggle OFF stops loop, human message interrupts;
   (e) Chat works normally with Bot Mode OFF;
   (f) No branding violations (Z-Dot only, no LPT mix).
4. Any known defects, TODOs, or unmerged work that would block a QA PASS?

Be factual — if it is NOT delivered or NOT complete, say so explicitly. Do not overstate readiness. This response feeds the official closure report and CEO escalation.

